For the participant with index 𝑖 , sex𝑖 encodes the participant's sex (male: 0, female: 1), age𝑖 is the participant's age. Under this model, 𝛽0 is the estimated regional CTh for a male of age 𝐴 , 𝛽1 is the between-sex difference in CTh at age 𝐴 , 𝛽2 is the rate at which CTh changes per year at age 𝐴 , while 𝛽3 and 𝛽4 model the sex-by-age interaction and quadratic age effects, respectively. Bootstrapping was used to estimate confidence intervals for the 5% and 95% percentiles of regional CTh variation.

